From: =?UTF-8?q?=E6=B2=90=E9=AA=81?= <lihantian.lht@antgroup.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 02:30:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat: server stop verifies port truth, kills orphans on
 confirm (v1.4.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

stopServerDaemon trusts only the pid in server.json, so orphan daemons
(killed half-starts, lost configs) could never be stopped and stop
would report success while the port stayed occupied — today's 401
incident class. stop now re-checks DEFAULT_PORT after stopping: show
the owner PID + command name, ask Y/N to kill, -y to skip the ask.
Non-TTY stdin is treated as N so agents never hang. Port lookup uses
netstat (win32) / lsof (POSIX); kill is taskkill /F on win32 and
SIGTERM→SIGKILL on POSIX.

killPidHard is async on purpose: the first sync-sleep version kept
hitting zombies (libuv never got an event-loop turn to reap after
SIGCHLD), misreporting live targets as alive.

Version 1.3.0→1.4.0. Note: installed CLI copies (setup.sh/npm) need a
reinstall to pick this up.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
